---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
import PageHero from "../components/PageHero.astro";
---
<Layout
  title="About"
  description="Deload is built by people who've written programs at 11pm and rewritten them by 7am. We're trying to give coaches their time back without taking the craft out of coaching."
>
  <PageHero
    title="Giving coaches their time back without taking the craft out of coaching."
    intro="One app for the whole coaching job: programming, roster, messages and the athlete's phone."
    wide
  />

  <section class="wrap pb-24">
    <div class="grid gap-12 border-t border-rule pt-12 lg:grid-cols-[minmax(0,1fr)_minmax(0,1.5fr)] lg:gap-16">
      <div>
        <p class="text-[1.75rem] font-semibold leading-tight tracking-[-0.03em] text-ink">Derek Miranda</p>
        <p class="mt-1 text-muted">Founder, Coach &amp; Athlete</p>
        <p class="mt-6 max-w-[42ch] text-muted">
          Two-plus years at Equinox, Precision Nutrition certified, then on my own with Sportslab NYC and Fitness360NYC, programming for gen-pop and weight-loss clients through marathoners, powerlifters and weightlifters.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="max-w-[62ch] space-y-6 text-[1.1875rem] leading-relaxed text-ink">
        <p class="text-[clamp(1.5rem,1.2rem+1vw,1.875rem)] font-medium leading-snug tracking-[-0.02em]">
          Deload started with my own roster. AI is powerful when the person driving it knows the craft, so I tried automating my programming, and it worked.
        </p>
        <p>
          The hard part was turning the draft into something you can run on the gym floor. Nobody had built a true agent for that, and it took an enormous amount of work.
        </p>
        <p>
          I think AI built for one niche is where this is heading. Coach burnout is high; if Deload takes that weight off and helps coaches' businesses grow, it's worth building.
        </p>
        <p>
          Deload is opinionated on purpose: it programs the way I'd program, edits the way I'd edit, and stays out of the way.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Layout>
